            "ImageDescription": {
              "value": "<p>18 <br>\n\"Elite\" Collection of <br>\nHardy Mums <br>\nFor Northern States, Splendid for the South also <br>\nAUNT MARY\u2014 Old Rose. <br>\nBABY\u2014 Yellow. <br>\nDIANA\u2014 QuiUed white. <br>\nERMALINDA\u2014 Deep pink. <br>\nEXCELSIOR\u2014 Deep yellow. <br>\nFIREBIRD\u2014 Red. <br>\nGOLDEN CLIMAX\u2014 Old gold. <br>\nLILLIAN DOTY\u2014 Pink. <br>\nTHE 8 FOR $1.19 <br>\ni <br>\nII* <br>\nAbove: LILLIAN DOTY <br>\nRight: EXCELSIOR. <br>\nNew Rose \"LORD CHARLEMONT.\" <br>\nNew Rose, <br>\n\"Lord <br>\nCharlemont\" <br>\nLORD CHARLEMONT\u2014 (H.T.) <br>\nBud very long-pointed; flower <br>\nlarge, full, high centered, per- <br>\nfectly shaped, clear crimson, <br>\ndeepening to carmine-crimson; <br>\nstrong fragrance. <br>\nOne Year, 40c each; <br>\nTwo Year, 75c. <br>\nHARDY SHRUBS OF QUALITY Full of Life\u2014 Sure to Grow <br>\nPLAN FOR FOUNDATION PLANTING n _ 1 - ANY OF THESE FOR FOREGROUND <br>\n, 25c each; .2.75 per dor, <br>\n, 20c each; .1.75 per doz. <br>\nt) 25c each; .2.50 per doz. <br>\n40c each; .4.50 per doz. <br>\n20c each; .1.75 per doz. <br>\n40c each; 4.50 per doz. <br>\nWhether planted individually or collectively Shrubs are an important feature in the adornment of any yard. The rich green of the <br>\n</p>\nsummer foliage plays a greater part in landscape effect than is often realized.",
